# g99-notify-producer -> DELETE-HOT (apps/desktop/src/main/index.ts) -- apply in the same step as native/core/crates/pending-wire/g99-notify-producer.wire,
# or every turn would notify twice.

The core decides and shows this PC's session notifications (host/notification/show) and sends the phone pushes. The TypeScript producer is removed.

## apps/desktop/src/main/index.ts
1. Delete `import { createDesktopTurnNotifier } from './desktop-turn-notifier';` and the whole `const turnNotifier = createDesktopTurnNotifier({ ... });`
   (with `nativeSessionTitleLabels` if nothing else reads it).
2. Delete `turnNotifier.dispose();` (shutdown), `turnNotifier.onSessions(sessions);`, `turnNotifier.onAgentPool(agents);` and the
   `unsubscribeTurnWaits = localService.subscribeSessionStates(... turnNotifier.onSessionState ...)` subscription with its unsubscribe in `unsubscribeTurnNotifier`.
3. `localService.readSessionFinalAnswer` loses its only caller here (check other callers, else delete it).
4. The host/notification/show handler already exists (notification-center.ts): the desktop's `isSessionOnScreen` / desktopPet check is answered by the host's
   foreground-thread report to the core (the audience's `host.foreground_thread`).

